ternate: move up 20, stab, move down 20, stab, move right, stab...\n\nHonestly, let me try a different screen with closer enemies. The north screen at slot 2: Link at bottom, Octoroks in middle. Let me march up while stabbing.\n\nLet me try: [{up+b,10},{up,15}] x 15 = 375 frames. Now Link sweeps upward stabbing.\n\nLet me do it and screenshot. From slot 2 (full hearts).\n\nBut first, is slot 2 still full hearts? I wrote 0x03D2=2 after loading slot2. That write may have messed with something. Let me reload slot 2 before the combat run.\n\nLet me reload slot 2 then run the sweep.\n\nActually hold on — maybe I should preserve my ability to do controlled damage rounds. Let me not worry.\n\nLet me reload slot 2 and do the sweep.\n\nActually, let me reconsider one more time. The differential for RUPEES is the most important anchor. Killing enemies is the way. Let's go.\n\nLet me also consider using the sword beam: Link only shoots beams when at full health. At full health, pressing B shoots a beam that can kill Octoroks from a distance — much safer! Great. So at full hearts, Link has the sword beam.\n\nSo from slot 2 (full hearts), pressing B fires a beam (if health full). The beam travels across the screen and kills Octoroks. This is safe and efficient.\n\nLet me do: from slot 2, hold B taps to fire beams, moving slightly. Beams fire one per B press.\n\nScript: [{b,4},{[],10}] x 20 = 280 frames. But direction matters; beams go the way Link faces (last direction). Let me face up first: {up,10} then fire.\n\nLet me do: {up,10}, then [{b,4},{[],12}] x15 = 240. Then screenshot.\n\nLet me reload slot 2 first."}
