f health RAM holds 5 (2.5 hearts) and you take damage, it draws 2 hearts. If I write health=2 (1 heart) and then take damage, it would draw 0.5 hearts. So I can test a candidate by write + damage + observe.\n\nI need the candidate. \n\n**Let me use the correlation across my existing snapshots.** I have snapshots at known heart states:\n- k0: full hearts (6)\n- k1: damaged (after hold-up; showed 2.5 → 5)  — but the equals-4 diff gave 0x03D2 6→4, so maybe it was 2 hits → 4.\nActually the screenshot showed 2.5 hearts → 5. But diff equals 5 found nothing in e1, equals 4 found 0x03D2. Contradiction → the HUD display and stored value may differ, or the screenshot showed 2.5 but actually it's 2.0 (hard to read).\n\nLet me not rely on my reading of hearts.\n\n**Better plan: get a rupee. Seriously.** Let me use the sword beam properly. The previous attempt failed because the enemies screen changed. Let me be careful.\n\nActually, from the CURRENT state (start screen, 2.5 hearts), let me go back north and shoot beams up at the Octoroks. But beams require FULL health; at 2.5 hearts Link can't shoot beams. Hmm.\n\nLet me reload slot 2 (full hearts, north screen) and carefully shoot beams. Don't press down at the end (that's what moved me).\n\nLet me redo the beam sweep without the final down, and check.\n\nActually, the beam only travels in a straight line and stops at the screen edge. Facing up from the bottom, it would hit the Octorok directly above. Good.\n\nLet me redo: reload slot 2, snapshot p0 again, then fire ~10 beams facing up.\n\nThen screenshot; check for a rupee or dead enemies.\n\nLet me do it."}
