e the game is in the \"damage\" state, using a save state at the damage moment.** I could save_state exactly when Link is being hit? Timing is hard.\n\nHmm.\n\n**Let me reconsider: maybe health is stored in the 0x03xx page and those weird 0x03D0-0x03D4 bytes ARE the health copies.** The routine at 0x8C4A writes 6 to them. Let me disassemble the actual routine at 0x8C00-0x8C60 properly. The earlier disassembly was misaligned/buggy. Let me disassemble from 0x8C00.\n\nActually, the trace said PC 0x8C43 and 0x8C4A. The instruction at 0x8C4A is `sec; rts` per the earlier (misaligned?) dump. Hmm.\n\nLet me disassemble from 0x8C00 length 96 and see.\n\nHmm, honestly, let me reconsider the strategy once more. Time is limited. \n\n**Radical simplification**: The user wants the addresses; the proof is a write + screenshot. Perhaps I'm overcomplicating the discovery. Let me use the strongest, simplest tool: **write a value to a candidate and see if the HUD shows it.**\n\nThe question is whether the HUD auto-updates. Let me TEST this with a value whose address I can find quickly and confidently — the hearts. \n\nTo find the hearts address, let me use a **very targeted differential**: take a snapshot at full health, then take damage (one hit), snapshot, and diff with \"decreased\" *restricted to the 0x0600-0x07FF range* by taking snapshots over that range only!\n\nsnapshot_memory has address and length parameters! I can snapshot only 0x0600-0x07FF (length 0x200). Then diffs only consider that range. \n\nLet me do: snapshot hh0 over 0x0600 length 0x200 at full health, take a hit, snapshot hh1, diff decreased.\n\nThat will avoid OAM/zero-page noise.\n\nBut wait, the earlier f1 diff already included 0x06xx addresses and equals-5 found only 0x0611. Hmm, but \"decreased\" over 0x0600 wouldn't include position noise much. Let me just do it to be sure, but with a clean single hit.\n\nActually the real problem: I need a reliable SINGLE hit and an accurate read of the heart display.\n\nLet me set up a controlled hit on the tree screen (slot 1) where there's one Octorok: walk into it.\n\nHmm.\n\nActually, let me reconsider — maybe the hearts are stored as **half-hearts at 0x066F or similar** and the value is large-ish. At 2.5 hearts, 0x066F=33 (0x21). Hmm, 33? If full = 6, no.\n\nHmm wait, maybe 0x066F is not constant. Let me check: I read 0x066F=33 at 2.5 hearts. Let me now check at full health (slot 2 loaded). Currently we're on the inventory screen with 3 full hearts... but that might be max-hearts display.\n\nUgh.\n\nNew decisive plan: **Find hearts by watching what changes when Link takes damage, restricted to 0x0600-0x07FF, with a clean single hit.**\n\nLet me do this carefully:\n1. Load slot 2 (full hearts). Actually slot 2 is the Leever screen with many enemies — hard to control single hit.\n   Better: create a controlled arena. Let me use the tree screen. Load slot 1 (tree screen, full hearts, Octoroks at known spots).\n2. Snapshot A over range 0x0600 length 0x200.\n3. Walk into an Octorok (single contact hit).\n4. Screenshot to confirm hearts changed by 0.5.\n5. Snapshot B over 0x0600.\n6. diff A/B decreased.\n\nLet me do it. Slot 1 = tree screen full hearts.\n\nActually, hmm, slot 1 was saved much earlier and might have been overwritten? Slots persist in the bridge session. slot 1 was saved at the tree screen. Should be fine.\n\nLet me load slot 1.\n\nWait, but in the tree screen, the Octoroks are at the right and I'm at the left; walking right, I might take multiple hits. Let me instead walk straight into the nearest enemy.\n\nAlternatively, use slot 2 but position Link carefully. Meh.\n\nLet me just use slot 1 and hold right until a hit, with snapshots around it. Since I snapshot the 0x0600 range only, and the \"decreased\" filter, the health byte should appear with a clear 6→5.\n\nLet me go.\n\nActually, let me improve: I'll take the BEFORE snapshot, then move right, and I need the AFTER snapshot at the moment of the hit. If I overshoot (multiple hits), the health goes 6→4 or less, still a decrease. The issue is other 0x06xx state also changing (Link x, enemy positions). But the heart byte should be a small value decreasing.\n\nLet me do it and look at the 0x06xx decreased list.\n\nLoad slot 1."}
