e needs 100 rupees... no. BUT there's a cave with a rupee worth 100? no.**\n\nHmm, what about the **\"Take any one\" cave**? Not in this area.\n\nOK let me get the sword.\n\nPlan:\n1. load clean file.\n2. Navigate to cave (we know: from start screen, the cave is the black rect at upper-left of clearing; earlier: left 50, up 60 from Link's post-up position).\nActually earlier from the fresh start (Link at center), I did: up 100 → went to north screen (oops). Then down 100 → back to start near cave. Then left 50 + up 60 → cave. So the cave entrance is at the top-left of the start screen, and walking straight up goes to the north screen through a different opening.\n\nSo from fresh start: left ~60 frames to x~64, then up to enter the cave.\n\n3. In the cave, wait for the text, then walk up onto the sword, confirm with a screenshot, then check the inventory (Start).\n\nLet me do it.\n\nActually, hmm, when I entered the cave before, I did left 50 + up 60, and the cave interior appeared with the text. Then up 90 put Link at the sword. The screenshot showed Link overlapping the sword. Then I pressed down 150 and exited. The inventory was empty.\n\nHmm, maybe I need to press A or just be exactly on it. Let me redo and after up 90, screenshot; then press Start to check the inventory WITHOUT leaving.\n\nLet me do it.\n\nActually, maybe the issue: the game requires Link to be at the sword's tile AND the text finished. In my sequence I waited 120 frames (text finished). Then up 90. Should be fine.\n\nUnless... the sword pickup requires pressing the \"A\"/B? No.\n\nWait, maybe Link DID get the sword but the inventory B box just doesn't show the sword icon in this ROM/screenshot rendering? Let me look at the inventory screenshot again: the B box (top-left square) is empty, and there's text \"USE B BUTTON FOR THIS\". In Zelda 1, the sword icon appears in that box. Hmm, but maybe the empty box means we don't have it.\n\nActually, in the inventory screenshot, the box shows nothing (black interior). Hmm.\n\nBut actually — hold on! In the very first cave screenshot, the sword was on a pedestal... and Link walked up and the screenshot showed him at the sword. Then I pressed down. Maybe the pickup happened but the inventory needs a redraw. \n\nLet me test combat directly: with the sword, walking into an Octorok and pressing B should kill it. Let me just try again on the tree screen: get close and press B. If the Octorok dies, we have the sword.\n\nHmm, earlier attempts showed Octoroks not dying.\n\nLet me just redo the cave and check the inventory.\n\nLet me do it now.\n\nActually, let me reconsider: is it possible the cave I entered is NOT the sword cave? The text \"IT'S DANGEROUS TO GO ALONE! TAKE THIS.\" IS the sword cave. And the sword was there. So it should work.\n\nMaybe the pickup requires Link to be at the sword's exact pixel and he stopped short. In the screenshot, Link's sprite was directly below the sword, overlapping slightly. Let me push up more.\n\nLet me redo: load clean, get to cave, wait, then hold up 150 frames (push against the sword as far as possible), then check inventory.\n\nLet me go."}
